WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.802
The debt limit crisis finally over.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:03.903
This morning

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.973
on this vote, the yeas are 63,

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:08.441
the nays are 36.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.609
The 60 vote threshold

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:10.977
having been achieved.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.313
The bill is passed

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.447
with just days to spare.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:14.848
The Senate

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.016
passing that debt limit deal

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:16.916
late last night

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.985
and preventing an economic catastrophe.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:19.652
President

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.354
Biden is now set to sign the bill

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.356
and address the nation later today.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.290
At the White House, Senate

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:24.924
Majority Leader

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:25.558
Chuck Schumer

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.361
giving a thumbs up after the deal passed.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.330
He's also been building this as a victory

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.865
for Democrats

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.801
House Republicans were ready

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.669
to take default hostage

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.005
in order to pass a radical hard

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.240
right agenda

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.474
that never could have passed

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.942
with the American people.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.645
So many of the destructive provisions

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.348
in the Republican bill are gone.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.451
This bill was a total rejection of what

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.986
the Republicans wanted

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.320
And look at the vote

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.321
that proves

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.657
that our strategy was the right strategy.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.059
That strategy, though,

00:00:59.059 --> 00:00:59.926
was rejected

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.195
by some members of his own party,

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.497
some Senate Democrats refusing to vote

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.565
to support that agreement.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.135
We should never have been put

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.071
in this position to begin with.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.739
This is about paying the ransom

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.941
to a bunch of hostage takers.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.209
And that is not how

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.310
we should run this government.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:17.844
It's not good

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.180
for the people of this country.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:20.914
CNN congressional

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:21.648
correspondent Lauren

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.049
Fox joins us live from Capitol

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:23.850
Hill this morning.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.619
So the debt limit deal ends up with

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.322
decent bipartisan support in the House

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.623
and the Senate.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.126
What is the feeling there this morning?

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.260
Well, it's a coalition

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.463
that you probably are going to see again.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.298
Erica, as the year drags on.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.099
That's because you have

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.233
divided government here.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.469
You have a House of Representatives

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.370
controlled by Republicans.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.339
You have Democrats controlling the Senate

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.207
and the White House.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.408
And I just want to go back

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.375
to the

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:52.412
amazing feat last night in the US Senate,

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.980
not because they passed that,

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.715
but because they were doing it.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:56.883
So quickly.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.918
They had about a dozen amendment votes

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.353
and one after another.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:00.920
Chuck Schumer,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.622
the majority leader, was keeping track

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.724
of how long each vote was taking.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.459
I just want to tell the American people,

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.827
usually the U.S.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.130
Senate does not move that quickly.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:10.864
Typically,

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.298
it takes them about an hour,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.533
sometimes even more,

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.301
to have a single vote last night.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.536
They kept members on the floor.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:17.670
They were trying to move through

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.172
about a dozen amendments

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.373
very expeditiously.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.074
Finally,

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:24.010
they got there shortly before midnight.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.712
But one thing that became very clear

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.412
last night,

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:27.981
this is a bipartisan coalition

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.149
you're going to see again

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.183
at the end of September.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.918
Lawmakers are going to have to pass

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:32.986
their spending bills.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.053
We also know

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.522
they have to pass a farm bill.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.090
They made some assurances last night

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.491
that there could be another

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.660
supplemental spending bill for Ukraine.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.896
So this is a bipartisan coalition

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.497
that is going to have to come together

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.632
on Capitol Hill again.

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:46.199
And again

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.001
because we're in divided government.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.769
Erica, as we noted, we're going to hear

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.771
from the president later today.

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:52.472
But the White House

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:55.341
has actually been fairly quiet this week.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.209
It seems like.

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:58.978
Yeah, but, you know,

00:02:58.978 --> 00:02:59.312
one thing

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.513
that we certainly can hear this morning

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.848
are the sighs of relief

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.249
from White House officials,

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.585
not only because this legislation

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:07.820
averts a potential default

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.422
that could have come as early as Monday,

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:09.889
but also

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.291
because it really helps

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.359
to smooth the path for this White House

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.795
over the rest of President Biden's term.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:18.331
That's because this bill incentivizes

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.900
Congress to pass regular government

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.669
funding bills by the end of the year

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.103
to avert a government shutdown

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.605
or face across the board

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:26.239
to defense

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.540
and non-defense

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.643
cuts of about 1% to the budget next year.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.345
That's a major piece

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.379
that White House officials

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.547
have been stressing to me

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.915
as one of the major

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.483
benefits of this bill.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.585
Now, listen, President Biden,

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:40.453
he put out a statement last night

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.088
hailing this as a major win

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:43.223
for the American people

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.757
and for the economy.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.393
And he also said that America is a nation

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.661
that pays its bills

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.063
and that this vote proves

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.731
that this bipartisan vote.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.566
He thanked the Senate majority

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.767
leader, Chuck Schumer in the Senate

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:55.868
Minority Leader,

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.636
Mitch McConnell,

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:58.905
for passing this bill quickly

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.273
and getting it through.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.774
And he now looks forward

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.643
to signing this bill as soon as possible.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.978
We're told that that could happen

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.412
as early as today.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.547
But as you mentioned tonight,

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.015
President Biden will address

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:09.782
the American people

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.151
from the Oval Office at seven p. M.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.820
This will be his first address

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.521
to the nation from the Oval Office.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.957
Certainly something to watch for.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:18.691
Jeremy, yesterday

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.592
we saw the president

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.560
take what appeared

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.361
to be a pretty hard

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:22.328
fall at that commencement

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.097
speech at the Air Force.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:24.797
How is he doing?

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:25.732
We know he made a joke of it.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:26.833
He made a lot of light of it.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.067
But do we know how he's doing?

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.136
Well, the White House says

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.272
that he is totally fine,

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:33.006
that he

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:34.907
simply tripped over that sandbag

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.277
that was left on the stage after.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.044
And we should note that

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:38.711
this came after

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:39.679
he shook hands

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.715
and saluted cadets for over 90 minutes

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:43.583
on stage yesterday,

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.084
hundreds of those cadets.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.085
But the president did indeed

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:46.986
make light of it.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.921
You can see how he's doing for yourself.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:49.522
Take a look at

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:50.556
how he returned to the White House

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.291
last night.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.259
He says he's

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.962
got sandbagged

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.937
And you see the president there

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.272
doing a little bit of a two

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.373
step there to show folks

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.709
that he's doing just fine.

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:11.177
That's how the White House is doing

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:12.879
and looks that way to fail

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:14.580
to set the sandbag shuffle.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.015
We'll come up with lots of names for it.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:16.716
Jeremy, Laura,

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:17.850
nice to see you about this morning.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.318
Thank you.

